/P 133 0 R
/E (If not addressed, a lack of clear regulation could lead to misuse and ethical lines being crossed. Inequalities may worsen and health risks will compound. In addition to individual patients suffering, there could be an overall loss of public trust in medicine systems. Governments will greatly gain from structured advice and encouragement on regulations, and techniques that they can employ to mitigate any detrimental effects. Ultimately, it is up to the WHO to debate and come to a consensus on a framework that can help guide countries as they navigate this quickly evolving landscape of genetic engineering technologies.)
/Pg 22 0 R
